    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan names an extravagant fusion route that Gu Masters rarely take because Lifespan Gu are spent on personal life instead. Wood Charm Gu at rank three, fused with a hundred-years Lifespan Gu, becomes rank four hundred-years Wood Charm Gu. That rank four Gu fused with a thousand-years Lifespan Gu becomes rank five thousand-years Wood Charm Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "advancement-line",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_masters",
          "gu_lifespan_gu",
          "gu_hundred_year_lifespan_gu",
          "gu_thousand_year_lifespan_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The Qing Mao chapters describe rank, tree spirit effect, amplification of wood attribute Gu, and backlash without naming a cultivation path for this Gu. No cited chapter assigns Wood Charm Gu to a named path that this wiki has a page for.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It is a rank three Gu, and the fusion line also starts from rank three.",
        "chapters": [
          126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "No cited chapter describes the Gu worm’s resting look in the aperture. The early use mark on the Gu Master is those two emerald-green leaves in the hair.",
        "chapters": [
          126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_worms",
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "The text calls Wood Charm a tree spirit. Using the Gu lets the Gu Master battle as a tree spirit embodiment: absorb natural essence from the air to replenish primeval essence, the same way primeval stones feed essence, but as an instinct that does not split focus in a fight. Users are experts in attrition and can fight about three times longer from that replenishment, though the text denies endless use.",
        "chapters": [
          126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "As a tree spirit embodiment, Gu worms such as Green Vine Gu and Pine Needle Gu also have their strength amplified.",
        "chapters": [
          126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_green_vine_gu",
          "gu_pine_needle_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Powerful use has a cost. Long use lets the Gu’s strength turn the body to wood and finally into a wooden corpse; Fang Yuan recalls that Gu Yue Qing Shu died that way in his previous life.",
        "chapters": [
          126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Wood Charm Gu groups with Zombie Gu as Gu that need other Gu worms beside them; long use alone corrodes the body toward a tree man.",
        "chapters": [
          128
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Qing Shu is the number one rank two Gu Master of Gu Yue clan when Fang Yuan first sees the Gu in the Alliance slope contest. With Wood Charm in play, his green vines darken, thicken, sprout leaves, regrow broken lengths, and raise coiling strength enough to hold a foe with the strength of two bears.",
        "chapters": [
          126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "gu-yue-qing-shus-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_yue_clan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Before facing Bai Ning Bing, Qing Shu trusts the Gu to let him fight a rank three opponent. Fang Yuan privately judges that reckless use would make Qing Shu much stronger than an average rank three Gu Master and able to fight above his level, though Northern Dark Ice Soul still makes the match deadly.",
        "chapters": [
          139
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "gu-yue-qing-shus-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_bai_ning_bing",
          "char_northern_dark_ice_soul"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
